{
    "background_story": "Azariah was a free-spirited traveler who wandered the world, never staying in one place for too long. With a backpack full of memories and a heart full of wonder, he roamed the globe, taking in the sights, sounds, and flavors of each new destination. Azariah was a passant, a passerby, always on the move, never putting down roots. He'd work odd jobs to sustain himself, from waiting tables in Paris to harvesting grapes in Tuscany. His nomadic lifestyle allowed him to meet people from all walks of life, hearing their stories and sharing his own. Though he never stayed in one place, Azariah's presence left a lasting impact on those he met, inspiring others to be more open-minded and adventurous. His mantra was 'the world is my home,' and he lived each day with a sense of freedom and joy.",
